Here is the commit message:
ACCUMULO-4191 Wrapped runnable with Trace.wrap in
 TabletServerBatchWriter to prevent loss of sendMutation events

Closes apache/accumulo#94

Signed-off-by: Josh Elser <elserj@apache.org>

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the loss of `sendMutation` events during the execution of mutations in the `TabletServerBatchWriter` class. This likely occurred due to the lack of a tracing mechanism that would capture and log the execution context of the `Runnable`, resulting in missed event tracking and difficulties in debugging mutation operations.

Here is the patch:

     void queueMutations(final MutationSet mutationsToSend) throws InterruptedException {
       if (null == mutationsToSend)
         return;
-      binningThreadPool.execute(new Runnable() {
+      binningThreadPool.execute(Trace.wrap(new Runnable() {

         @Override
         public void run() {
           if (null != mutationsToSend) {
             try {
               log.trace("{} - binning {} mutations", Thread.currentThread().getName(), mutationsToSend.size());
               addMutations(mutationsToSend);
             } catch (Exception e) {
               updateUnknownErrors("Error processing mutation set", e);
             }
           }
         }
-      });
+      }));
     }



